  "body": "In the [previous version of Web App Manifest](https://www.w3.org/TR/2020/WD-appmanifest-20200714/#obtaining), the credentials mode is determined by:\r\n\r\n> If the manifest link's crossOrigin attribute's value is \"use-credentials\", then set request's credentials mode to \"include\". Otherwise, set request's credentials mode to \"omit\".\r\n\r\nNow the Web App Manifest spec is using [the algorithm defined in the HTML spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#link-type-manifest), which says:\r\n\r\n> Set request's credentials mode to the CORS settings attribute credentials mode for el's crossorigin content attribute.\r\n\r\nThe [CORS settings attribute credentials mode](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-settings-attribute-credentials-mode) is either \"same-origin\"(no CORS or anonymous) or \"include\"(use-credentials) in my understanding. Thus the default credentials mode is \"same-origin\" rather than \"omit\".\r\n\r\nDid I misunderstand anything?\r\n ",
